  "problem": "$\\operatorname{sinh}\u2061(\\operatorname{ln}\u2061\\sqrt{2})=$",
  "worked_solution": "The definition of $\\operatorname{sinh}\u2061x$ is \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sinh}\u2061x=\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sinh}\u2061(\\operatorname{ln}\u2061\\sqrt{2}) & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{\\operatorname{ln}\u2061\\sqrt{2}}-{e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}\u2061\\sqrt{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{\\operatorname{ln}\u2061\\sqrt{2}}-{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(1/\\sqrt{2})}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\sqrt{2}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{2-1}{\\sqrt{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
